          "version": "original",
          "lines": [
            1,
            676
          ],
          "empty_file_read": false,
          "assessment": "Full 676 lines. Actual ASRF/FSIGN runtime imports with local YAML contracts, not executed. ASRF fixtures distinguish direct/transitive/mutual authorization cycles from disconnected cycles and reject malformed empty/whitespace identities, with finite ledger counts; identities and caller-supplied graph are trusted declarations, and early sha256 labels are only32hex. FSIGN checks specific2x2/4x4 stoquastic matrices, nonnegative finite weights, identical-spin attractive determinantal hypotheses, and exact sign-reversing weight-preserving involutions with negative coverage. Several malformed involutions and unequal hypotheses are genuine negative controls. Odd C3 alternation is a restricted gauge obstruction, not general FSP hardness. C3 gap claim uses one hardcoded64-state host; the U5 negative also drops bonds so does not isolate U. Float contamination and unsupported prose are explicit refusals. Nonclaim attribute/text checks do not prove completeness. The final pipeline independently accepts a named fock_space_state_64 authorization declaration and an unrelated2x2 matrix; no candidate or certificate content is carried between them. No native gap computation or physical result reproduced."
        }
      ]
    },
