      "assessment": "Full 285 lines, including re-read 86-200 after one output truncation. One FD-strengthening example checks implication and step counts, not the claimed cell-partition inclusion; eight shuffled dependency orders compare actual terminal cell partitions under early_exit=False for one chain. The purported infinite cyclic TGD example consists of trivial MVDs A->>B and B->>A on heading AB, with no fresh existential symbols; assertions merely require a result and <=100 rows, never exhaustion. Minimal-cover assertions check only two determinants and length, omitting dependent attributes and closure equivalence. Antichain positive is finite. Nested-record round trip, unique-version latest-event reduction, projected shard key, hash-to-64-set union, split sum and prefix ordering are test-local examples; the mock HLL has no registers/cardinality estimator and is not HyperLogLog validation. Quantile scale test adjusts width/tolerance but checks only both routes, not scaled estimates. Equal-version conflicting CDC events and arbitrary event semantics are untested.",
