      "assessment": "Full 216 lines. Thirty insert/delete samples check bucket/count conservation using actual inserted values. Thirty uniform random samples of size 100 compare estimated median to the mean of the two middle values and assert a bucket-width error bound. That bound is false for separated clusters: bounded AST control C037 yields 10 versus independent median 500 with width 10. The tolerance verifier itself recomputes true quantiles and can refuse, so this does not show false Repair. Below-error routing is conditional on error > .05. SQLite tests use forty western inserts and fifteen initial deletions, accept repair within tolerance or tight-tolerance fallback, but reuse the evaluator true-median helper instead of an independent oracle and do not bind arbitrary sketch counts to a source partition.",
