      "assessment": "Full 368 lines. Local minimum-rotation function enumerates all rotations (not Booth linear algorithm) and accepts periodic0101 and empty string as Lyndon; C052 confirms a nontrivial equal rotation, contradicting strict definition. Correct finite rotation invariance remains useful for necklace representatives. TBNF identifiers admit underscore (37 characters despite Sigma36 wording) and empty identifiers; bodies are unconstrained, and a separate balanced-bracket helper ignores all nonbrackets. Graph hash is only a sorted degree multiset, not WL refinement or complete isomorphism certification; same-degree nonisomorphic graphs collide. SPJA test checks literal conjunct inclusion, no chase, and core query is assigned []; missing-vs-None ambiguity remains if arbitrary values allowed. Float refusal alone admits every non-float type, so is not an exact-rational carrier check. Fraction telescoping sum and one projection kernel equality are exact examples. Flattening never unflattens despite roundtrip description. Quantum nondistributivity is mathematically explained but tests unequal strings; CHSH only evaluates2sqrt2, while global section/Wigner consistency/separability are assigned booleans without states or observables. No production imports.",
