      "assessment": "Full 966 lines in three contiguous displayed chunks. All sketch classes are test-local. Integer Count-Min updates are conservative only for nonnegative updates and compatible hashes; width/depth/seed validity not enforced, merge accepts different salts and reconstructs default seed. C039 confirms count7 becomes0 merging same-seed1 sketch with empty. Cuckoo insertion evicts using Python integer hash but lookup uses SHA-derived alternate index; C040 finds successful insertion makes admitted keys unfindable. Sparse HLL transition/commutative max register example is real; its identity assertion compares the same merge computation to itself and associativity is absent. T-digest error tests use uniform grids and normalized value error, not arbitrary-distribution rank bounds. Reservoir2000runs, HLL one cardinality, Bloom100members/nonmembers, Count-Min3keys+500noise and Space-Saving one ordered stream are samples, not probability guarantees. Median test sorts every window despite heap description. Sliding/tumbling sum, watermark max, tombstone overwrite and signed Counter cancellation are exact local examples; session merge does not test associativity, delta-join case has empty cross-delta intersection, and outer join emissions are handwritten. DGIM uses only one window-length stream so no real expiry case; no generated value-object strict-type controls despite headline. No production streaming implementation is exercised.",
