      "assessment": "Full 578 lines. Entirely test-local dataclasses/arithmetic. Morphism construction validates nothing, accepts partial/foreign/duplicate maps, compares tuple presentation while composition sorts: valid two-attribute unsorted maps violate declared identity equality (C041). Existing associativity example composes to empty maps, so provides no nonempty chain coverage. Simplex checks duplicate vertices and two face identities, not a category nerve or invalid face indices. Dictionary restriction and one compatible merge illustrate the sheaf-of-assignments case but asserted uniqueness is a single chosen candidate; presheaves do not generally satisfy sheaf gluing. Ring sums measure one cohomology-class obstruction, not the dimension/vanishing of an entire H1 group. Sieve test prefixes strings and checks length, Kan pushforward renames rows, stalk selects a tuple, Galois test checks one inclusion, homotopy colimit is symmetric difference; none implements the named universal property. Explicit integer Cech cancellation, scalar inverse holonomy, Set characteristic function and Z10 kernel/image are valid finite calculations. Nonzero-curvature comment actually supplies zero holonomy defect. Persistent barcodes/Betti numbers/Euler subdivision counts are assigned constants, not computed homology; PD examples require their closed orientable/coefficient context. Rips example constructs edges and checks one triangle clique, not all dimensions. No production imports/native execution.",
